Time-of-Flight Technology Improves Distance Measurement

ToF sensors calculate distance using the travel time of emitted light reflected from a target. Compact modules can combine a laser emitter, receiver, optics and signal-processing electronics to support integration into industrial equipment and embedded systems.

Performance depends on measurement range, repeatability, response time, ambient-light immunity and laser safety.

Robotics and Automation Expand Applications

Manufacturers use ToF sensors for robot positioning, object detection, conveyor monitoring and warehouse automation. Smart devices and connected equipment also use compact distance sensors for presence detection and spatial awareness.

